Verifies that a physical replicant takes the skip-recovery path when a rewind
unwinds no commit, and stays consistent afterwards.

With log_cksum_prev off a physrep can only anchor on a commit, and with
physrep_skip_noop_truncation off it always rewinds to that anchor.  Forcing
re-registration while the source writes large transactions leaves the physrep
mid-transaction, so it truncates the uncommitted tail back to its last applied
commit: exactly the skip-recovery case.

The test checks that every rewind took the skip path (no full recovery), that
the physrep keeps applying and matches the source, that it recovers cleanly
after kill -9, and that a comdb2ar copy of the physrep taken across rewinds
succeeds and restores.
